DEPENDENCIES

  * OCaml 5.3.0;
  * ocamlfind (>= 1.4.0);
  * Lablgtk (>= 2.18.0);
  * Lablgtk.rsvg (for graph viewer support);
  * xml-light (>= 2.5);
  * yojson (>= 2.1);
  * atdgen (>= 2.12);
  * ocp-indent (>= 1.8.0);
  * ocp-index (>= 1.3.6);
  * merlin (>= 5.5);
  * ocamldiff (>= 1.2);
  * ocurl (for remote file editing via SFTP);
  * inotify (file system notifications);
  * Dot command (optional, for module dependencies graph visualization).



HOW TO COMPILE

  Ensure all dependencies are installed via OPAM:

    opam install ocaml ocamlfind lablgtk ocp-indent ocp-index xml-light yojson \
                 atdgen ocamldiff merlin inotify ocurl

  Change to the OCamlEditor toplevel directory and execute:

    ocaml build.ml ocamleditor

  If the native code compiler is not available on your platform, compile with:

    ocaml build.ml ocamleditor-bytecode

  The name of the executable is "ocamleditor.opt" (or "ocamleditor" if native
  compilation is not supported), which can be found in the "src" directory.



INSTALLATION

  To install OCamlEditor, execute:

    ocaml build.ml install [-prefix <path>]

  By default, the executable is installed under "/usr/local/bin", icons under
  "/usr/local/share/ocamleditor/icons", and plugins under
  "/usr/local/share/ocamleditor/plugins". You can specify an alternative
  installation prefix with the `-prefix` option.

  To uninstall:

    ocaml build.ml uninstall [-prefix <path>]



DEVELOPMENT

  The main page for development is hosted on Github, see the
  project's page:

    https://github.com/ftovagliari/ocamleditor
















